WEBVTT

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.650
Abeno-san?

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.100
Abeno-san!

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.150
Are you okay? Wake up!

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.660
Abeno-san!

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.780
Abeno-san!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.780
Huh?

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.290
Huh?

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.790
Is he asleep?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.100
Abeno-san, please wake up!

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.760
Summon...

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.550
The Mononokean. I'll summon it.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.980
Momonokean, come.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.380
You can't even say it right.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.960
So it comes even if you say it wrong...

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.630
<b>Mystery 3: Zenko</b>

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.750
Where's your house?

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.520
It's a flower shop called 
"Hana Ashi" in Suzaku-cho.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.730
You heard him. Can we get there?

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.760
I guess the front door will do.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.390
Are you half asleep?

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.270
Opening door to "Hana Ashi" in Suzaku-cho

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.270
"Opening door to 'Hana Ashi'"?

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.210
Whoa! Is this...

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.540
the front door to my house?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.490
If you open it, you'll be home.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.240
H-Hello.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.590
How does this thing work?

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:13.150
That hanging scroll expresses 
the Mononokean's will as text.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.290
Its will?

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.540
"Mononokean"...

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.470
In other words, this tearoom itself is a yokai.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.490
What?!

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:31.850
Nice to meet you, Hanae.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.420
N-Nice to meet you, too.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.430
Just leave.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.840
We've got work tomorrow...

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.980
Did Itsuki open two portals 
to the Underworld?

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.980
"Did Itsuki open two portals 
to the Underworld?"

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.260
He opened one each for Big 
Boss Scree and its babies.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:44.920
<i>Come to think of it, he said he 
could only open it twice a day.</i>

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.240
<i>Speaking of things he said...</i>

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.400
Did a yokai used to be 
the master of this place?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:54.250
Why is Abeno-san the master now?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.460
That's because the medicine—

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.400
Ashiya!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.460
Yes, sir!

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.400
Quit flapping your gums and go home.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.520
I-I'll be going, then.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.720
Oh, welcome home. You're back late.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.260
I-I'm home.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.730
<b>♥ Congratulations ♥ 
First Classroom
Experience</b>

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.230
Are you okay?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.080
You seem tired.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.260
What were you doing at school?

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.670
N-Nothing.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.920
<i>Exorcising yokai, Mom.</i>

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>I know I have a debt to pay, but...</i>

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.130
I don't think I can keep this up.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.250
<i>Is high school that hard?</i>

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.620
<i>But Fuzzy and Big Boss 
Scree seemed pretty happy.</i>

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.680
<i>It's hard work, but maybe it's worth doing.</i>

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.010
You worked hard today.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.570
Bye, sir.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.280
Make sure you do your homework.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.660
<i>Maybe he isn't feeling well.</i>

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.720
Ashiya!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.960
Oh, uh...

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.590
I'm Saga. This is Fusshi.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.910
Hello.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.650
Saga-kun and Fusshi-kun.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.920
You can lose the "kun."

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.270
You need notes from the 
days you missed, right?

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.360
You can borrow ours.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.680
Sorry about the bad handwriting.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.440
Thank you!

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.680
Huh?! Don't cry!

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.880
Where do you live, Ashiyan?

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.000
Suzaku-cho.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.820
That's the same direction as us.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.370
Let's walk home together.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.150
Okay!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.680
I'm hungry.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.300
<i>That's right! I'd forgotten because 
of the yokai incidents, but this is it!</i>

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:49.870
Wanna stop by a convenience store?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:50.820
Yeah, let's go!

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.370
What should we get?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.200
<i>This is the high school life I wanted!</i>

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.700
We can decide when we get there.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.390
What's wrong, Ashiyan?

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.710
Uh, I just...

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.710
I just remembered I have something to do!

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.730
We'll walk home together another time.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:07.560
Bye!

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.560
Later.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.100
What a weird dude.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.720
You can't just connect the 
classroom to here on a whim!

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.430
I was worried because you weren't at school!

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.500
Not so loud.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.400
You're being rude to our guest.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.480
A guest?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.600
This is Mitsuchigura-sama. 
He's here seeking our help.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.990
I thank you, I thank you.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.280
No, thank you.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.940
Shut up and read this.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.120
<b>A Dog of Flanders</b>

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.120
<b>For Ages 5 And Up</b>

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.610
Nello!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:43.610
Hey...

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.080
You've only read the first couple of pages.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.640
When I think of the final scene...

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.010
Oh, no... I can't...

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.520
Well, as you can see, 
he's the right man for the job.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.830
Indeed.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.390
What's going on here?

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.890
I cannot express emotions on my own.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.500
But when I wear this "crying mask,"

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.040
as you can see, I can express the emotion.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.800
Wow, you're crying!

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:13.280
This is my "rage mask." 
It makes my emotions violent.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.160
What're you looking at, ya little punk?!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.910
Take it off! Please take it off!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:21.930
But when I had Abeno-sama 
exorcise me once before,

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:25.670
I dropped one of my masks in this world.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:29.130
You're the right man to go get it.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.170
Huh?

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:33.640
The mask I lost was my "laughing mask."

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.320
Whoever it possesses will be forced 
to laugh for the rest of their life.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.170
You mean they'll be laughing forever?

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.600
The only way to remove it

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.210
is to show the "laughing 
mask" a crying face.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.460
A crying face?

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.260
You're good at it.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.320
It's not a talent or anything!

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:55.570
Just go show the human possessed 
by the mask a crying face.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:00.380
A temple?

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:01.830
Huh?

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.090
Abeno-san, you're not coming?

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.250
You're just going to get a mask.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.840
A five-year-old can run errands by himself.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.660
I ran my first errand when I was four!

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.090
Who cares?

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:16.280
Don't underestimate the errand-running 
ability of a 15-year-old!

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.290
I'll be back!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.710
He seems quite reliable.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.600
How dare he treat me like a five-year-old?

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.600
Hey.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.800
But if I fail,

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.310
who knows what he'll say later?

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:29.800
Hey!

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.610
Yes?!

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:31.720
Huh?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.480
What are you doing over there?

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.990
I-It's a yokai!

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.740
Who are you calling a yokai?

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.120
<i>Oh, it's a little kid.</i>

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.750
What were you doing in the 
storage shed? Are you a thief?

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.650
No, actually. I'm just 
looking for a lost item.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.770
A lost item?

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.740
It's a mask of a laughing face.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.260
Have you seen it?

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.660
I clean this place every day,

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.390
but I haven't seen any such thing.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.730
When did you lose it?

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.390
When?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.890
<i>I forgot to ask.</i>

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.210
Stop trying to lie to me.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.650
If you come clean, I'll forgive you.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.990
<i>This grade school kid is disappointed in me!</i>

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.530
Dad's awake.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.080
Dad?

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.560
He's laughing again.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:21.370
He used to be a stubborn 
old man who rarely laughed.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.250
<i>That's gotta be it.</i>

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:30.040
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.050
My dad's been possessed by a yokai?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.300
That's why I'd like to see your dad.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.440
I was raised near a graveyard,

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.740
but I've never seen any ghosts or yokai.

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.560
Not once in the 15 years since I was born.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.570
What? 15 years?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.150
You're not in grade school? But you're so tiny!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.430
Not even a grade school kid 
would be fooled by your lies.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.270
You lie at a five-year-old's level.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.650
<i>Five again! Déjà vu!</i>

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.900
If you don't leave, I'm calling the police.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.390
Wait, wait!

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.740
You don't have to believe me about the yokai,

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.410
but I want you to believe me 
when I say I can help your dad!

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.160
"You don't have to believe me, 
but believe me?"

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.830
Either way, I have to believe you.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:17.210
Then you don't have to believe me, 
but just take my word for it...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.550
No, wait. How should I put it?

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.460
What's your name?

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.300
I'm Fujiwara Zenko.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.610
My name?

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:28.040
Ashiya... Ashiya Hanae.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.840
Hanae? That's a cute name.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.760
Okay, Hanae, follow me.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.150
You believe me, Zenko-chan?

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.950
Call me Zenko.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.870
I'll take your word for it,

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:48.710
so make me believe "yokai" actually exist.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.110
And...

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.460
Let's see you turn my dad back to normal.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.560
At least believe this, Zenko.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.220
I haven't told you a single lie.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.810
Dad, there's someone I want you to meet.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.290
Wh-Who...

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.070
are you?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.070
<i>That mark on his forehead is 
the same one that yokai had.</i>

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.670
<i>He is the one possessed 
by the "laughing mask."</i>

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.240
I-I'll kill you!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:24.920
Huh?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.160
I'll kill you, punk!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:30.330
If you're her boyfriend, I'll kill you!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.910
I-I'm not! You're mistaken!

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.000
He's not.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.460
He says he might be able 
to stop your laughter.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.530
What?

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.050
It's hard to explain,

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.360
but will you let me help you?

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.870
C-Can you really...

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.590
s-stop it?

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:49.980
Probably, yes.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.380
Then please. I...

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.480
can't even chant... sutras.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.300
Hanae.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.000
It wasn't a lie, right?

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:06.490
You can really turn him back to normal, right?

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.920
<i>She's trying to act and sound tough,</i>

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:13.750
<i>but she's actually been 
worried this whole time.</i>

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.500
<i>This girl is probably</i>

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.140
<i>not as strong as I thought.</i>

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:19.460
What?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.470
S-Sorry! It just happened!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.600
How dare you touch Zenko, you brat?!

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.770
I'm sorry!

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.210
Huh? Wait...

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.980
He stopped laughing for a moment.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.090
Dad...

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.130
<i>This is really bad.</i>

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.080
I've been wondering...
What's with the picture book?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.320
Uh, I guess you could say it's
an item guaranteed to work?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.680
Huh.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:45.530
I'm not joking! I'm completely serious!

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:49.390
Ashiya-sama hasn't been 
working here long, has he?

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.170
I'm sorry you had to deal with him.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.430
He just needs more experience.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.750
I'm quite all right,

00:12:56.750 --> 00:13:02.520
but I can see on your face 
that you can't help worrying.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:08.550
Well, most jobs aren't this 
easy or well-suited for him.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:12.320
Surely he can handle this one himself.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:19.870
<i>It's not working.</i>

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:22.530
<i>I'm too conscious of my surroundings to cry.</i>

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:31.590
<i>I don't intend to let you 
take over this temple.</i>

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.580
First Academic and Career Survey
Class 3-1  Number 25  Student Fujiwara Zenko
Guardian Name_______Seal
Please circle your plans after graduating middle school.
(1.) High School   2. Work   3. Other
First Choice - Daiyuzan Public High School - Subject: Buddhism

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:35.580
What do you mean? You don't 
have anyone else to do it.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.840
Are you saying you can't count on me?

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.580
It's not that.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.840
I don't want to leave this 
temple to my daughter.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:46.340
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.040
<i>Is it because I'm your daughter?</i>

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:50.350
So you don't need to attend 
a Buddhist high school.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.350
<i>Because I'm a girl?</i>

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.120
Hey, wait! We're not finished talking!

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:54.940
I don't—

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.520
I understand. Say no more.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.680
I'll never mention taking 
over the temple again.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:10.320
"He found Nello collapsed on 
the ice-cold stone floor.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.600
Patrasche approached Nello,

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.540
and Nello embraced him."

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:13.950
<i>Is that a spell?</i>

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:16.990
<i>I can't believe I'm having this much trouble</i>

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:18.790
<i>showing a crying face to 
the "laughing mask."</i>

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:22.540
Maybe I should call Abeno-san.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:24.730
No, I can't!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.150
After grandstanding like that, 
I can't ask him for help!

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.520
Are you okay?

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.100
I'm having some trouble.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.460
Give me some time.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:36.560
Then, for a change of pace, 
will you help me tidy up the yard?

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.310
I want to finish before the sun sets.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.170
Could you pull the weeds in the yard?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.080
Okay.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:48.870
<i>A break might restore my tear glands.</i>

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:54.040
Do you clean the whole temple every day?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:54.980
Yeah.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:56.970
It must be hard to do on your own.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:59.470
Yeah, but I love this temple.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:04.210
<i>This temple full of memories, 
where I was born and raised.</i>

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:08.070
<i>I don't intend to let you 
take over this temple.</i>

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.470
Just look at all these weeds...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.060
Hey, wait! These are daffodils!

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.970
Daffodils? Those leaves?

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.990
I've been pulling all of them out.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:20.350
How could you do this?!

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:23.130
Stop cleaning the yard! 
We're going to replant these!

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.480
Uh, okay.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.010
Your hands will get dirty.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.660
I'll lend you a glove.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.740
I'll be fine. I'm used to it.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.070
The dirt is so dry.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.300
We'll need to water them later.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.690
You know a lot about gardening.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:41.820
My family runs a flower shop.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.500
Are you going to take over the 
flower shop in the future?

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:46.410
Huh?

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.760
That was my plan.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.140
I'm the eldest son,

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:56.040
and I know my mom worked
hard to open the shop,

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:59.880
but she said I didn't have to take over.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:00.520
Huh?

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:03.840
"Opening a flower shop was my dream,

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.020
so you don't have to take over.

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:09.560
You should follow your own path," she said.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:13.790
When I told my dad I'd take over the temple,

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.690
he refused my request.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:16.330
Huh?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:19.540
But his reason was totally 
different from yours.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.290
"I don't want to leave this temple 
to my daughter," he said.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:25.920
Zenko...

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.170
How is that different from my case?

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.490
It's completely different.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.780
He said I couldn't because I'm his daughter.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:34.460
Because I'm a girl.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.430
Oh, that's what he meant?

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.100
I thought he meant he didn't want

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.060
to force his own child 
to take over the temple.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:48.970
Not because I'm a girl, 
but because I'm his child?

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:53.820
Honestly, I think I was sort of 
relieved after my mom told me that.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.320
It meant it was okay for me 
to choose something else.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:17:00.830
<i>Choose something else...</i>

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:05.830
<i>Dad said that for my sake?</i>

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:13.240
I feel a little better after that yard work.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.470
I might be able to cry now.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.050
What's wrong, Zenko?

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:21.900
What?

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.810
"What"? You're crying!

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:29.060
What's wrong?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.470
<i>Why am I crying?</i>

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:32.860
<i>Because I'm happy?</i>

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.030
<i>No.</i>

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.560
<i>Because I'm sad?</i>

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:36.810
<i>No.</i>

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:40.770
<i>Because I'm angry at myself 
for being unable to consider</i>

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:42.450
<i>how my father felt.</i>

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:46.360
Are you okay?

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:47.960
Was it me? Is it my fault?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.960
If it is, I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.470
Z-Zenko.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.100
Wh...

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.840
What did you do to Zenko, you brat?!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.350
Dad!

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.900
<i>That's the "laughing mask"!</i>

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.750
<i>Oh, right. It's because he 
saw Zenko's crying face.</i>

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:16.780
Hanae?

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:21.280
<i>I can remove it now!</i>

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:25.790
Hanae?

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:29.420
I...

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.050
I got it!

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.110
Got what?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.660
The laughter stopped.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:34.420
Yes!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.820
Now I just need to give 
this back to the yokai.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:42.400
Don't think you'll get away 
with making Zenko cry!

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.770
Brace yourself!

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:46.240
Wait! Calm down, Father!

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.690
Fa—

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.690
You have no right to call me "Father"!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.690
Dad, don't!

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:55.440
Please excuse my employee.

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:58.430
I'll make sure he regrets it later,

00:18:58.430 --> 00:18:59.950
so will you let this slide?

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.310
Who the hell are you?

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.610
Abeno-san? What are you doing here?

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:06.920
You can't even handle a simple
errand, you five-year-old.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.460
We saw everything from in there.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:10.700
I thank you.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:11.580
When did you get there?!

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.390
You were inside the closet?

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:16.170
Hey.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:18.620
Let's go.

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:19.530
Yes, sir!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.840
<i>He looks like he wants to say something.</i>

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.540
I'll go get my shoes.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:30.110
<i>Making him work on his own 
wore me out even more.</i>

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.980
Who are you guys?

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.520
Do you feel like believing what he said now?

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:38.110
Huh?

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.880
That yokai really do exist in this world.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.020
I'll tell you who we are

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:48.040
when you truly believe.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:51.500
Thanks for waiting!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.560
Let's get out of here.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.880
I need my bag and the book, too.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:55.870
Hurry up.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:56.840
Okay.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.620
Hey, wait! You can't live inside my closet!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.080
Zenko.

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.660
Sorry for making you cry,

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.260
but I appreciate the help. Thanks.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:10.130
"Thanks"?

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:11.770
Don't run from me! Get out here!

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.610
Wh-What's going on?

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.930
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.610
Do you wish I'd been born a boy instead?

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:26.120
What kind of question is that?

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:30.870
I see.

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:40.820
<i>I had trouble believing in yokai, 
but I'm glad I believed Hanae.</i>

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.880
<i>Someday, I'll have to thank him properly.</i>

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.860
I hope I see Hanae again.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.020
What?!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.390
This is your payment.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.900
Thank you.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:56.570
Mononokean, our guest is leaving.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:00.900
Very well. Opening nijiriguchi.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.980
"Opening"... I can't read that.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:00.900
It's "nijiriguchi."

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:03.990
Oh, this thing?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.710
Hey, open the door.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:06.980
Yes, sir.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.080
My legs fell asleep...

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.310
I never tire of watching Ashiya-sama.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.960
I do.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:18.590
But your expression seems to have softened

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.180
since the last time we met.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.360
More like, since he arrived,

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:26.890
I've had more reasons to tense up.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.720
That's one of the factors in your change.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:33.680
I'm sure Ashiya-sama will make a good worker.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.230
You think so?

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.870
That's the Underworld. Stay inside.

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:38.940
The Underworld?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.710
Humans like him are invaluable.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:44.490
But that's also why you must be careful.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.490
Ashiya-sama is dangerous.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:50.740
You're right.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.150
I'll keep that in mind.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 4 "The Underworld"</b>

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:30.680
Abeno-san, there's something 
I've been wondering for a while.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:31.660
Can I ask you?

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:32.430
What?

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:35.640
Um, when did the Mononokean

00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:38.020
learn to use emoticons?

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.080
Don't ask me.
